--- BUF-19, BUF-21: byte 1 is the first byte, and a variable-indexed byte access reads and writes ---
a buffer called 'toolbox' is "z9rqteolp67cgefkr".
a number called 'toolbox first byte' is byte 1 of 'toolbox'.
If 'toolbox first byte' is not 122 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-19: expected 122 got {'toolbox first byte'}", Exit 95. Print 'toolbox first byte'.
a number called 'toolbox read position' is 16.
a number called 'toolbox byte at the variable position' is byte 'toolbox read position' of 'toolbox'.
If 'toolbox byte at the variable position' is not 107 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-21: expected 107 got {'toolbox byte at the variable position'}", Exit 95. Print 'toolbox byte at the variable position'.
Set byte 'toolbox read position' of 'toolbox' to 232.
a number called 'toolbox byte after the variable write' is byte 'toolbox read position' of 'toolbox'.
If 'toolbox byte after the variable write' is not 232 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-21: expected 232 got {'toolbox byte after the variable write'}", Exit 95. Print 'toolbox byte after the variable write'.

--- the same leaf, a different seed (a different length/position) ---
a buffer called satchel is "uxzdx9d6t9j389qsy".
a number called 'satchel first byte' is byte 1 of satchel.
If 'satchel first byte' is not 117 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-19: expected 117 got {'satchel first byte'}", Exit 95. Print 'satchel first byte'.
a number called 'satchel read position' is 14.
a number called 'satchel byte at the variable position' is byte 'satchel read position' of satchel.
If 'satchel byte at the variable position' is not 57 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-21: expected 57 got {'satchel byte at the variable position'}", Exit 95. Print 'satchel byte at the variable position'.
Set byte 'satchel read position' of satchel to 207.
a number called 'satchel byte after the variable write' is byte 'satchel read position' of satchel.
If 'satchel byte after the variable write' is not 207 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-21: expected 207 got {'satchel byte after the variable write'}", Exit 95. Print 'satchel byte after the variable write'.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a buffer called 'toolbox' is "z9rqteolp67cgefkr",
  a number called 'toolbox first byte' is byte 1 of 'toolbox',
  If 'toolbox first byte' is not 122 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-19: expected 122 got {'toolbox first byte'}", Exit 95. Print 'toolbox first byte',
  a number called 'toolbox read position' is 16,
  a number called 'toolbox byte at the variable position' is byte 'toolbox read position' of 'toolbox',
  If 'toolbox byte at the variable position' is not 107 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-21: expected 107 got {'toolbox byte at the variable position'}", Exit 95. Print 'toolbox byte at the variable position',
  Set byte 'toolbox read position' of 'toolbox' to 232,
  a number called 'toolbox byte after the variable write' is byte 'toolbox read position' of 'toolbox',
  If 'toolbox byte after the variable write' is not 232 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-21: expected 232 got {'toolbox byte after the variable write'}", Exit 95. Print 'toolbox byte after the variable write'.

--- BUF-23, BUF-24: a hex literal and a character literal both write the byte they name ---
a buffer called 'the drawer' is "nok6z243".
Set byte 1 of 'the drawer' to 0xE9.
a number called 'the drawer byte written by a hex literal' is byte 1 of 'the drawer'.
If 'the drawer byte written by a hex literal' is not 233 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-23: expected 233 got {'the drawer byte written by a hex literal'}", Exit 95. Print 'the drawer byte written by a hex literal'.
Set byte 7 of 'the drawer' to 'b'.
a number called 'the drawer byte written by a character literal' is byte 7 of 'the drawer'.
If 'the drawer byte written by a character literal' is not 98 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-24: expected 98 got {'the drawer byte written by a character literal'}", Exit 95. Print 'the drawer byte written by a character literal'.
Print 'the drawer byte written by a character literal'.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a buffer called 'the drawer' is "nok6z243",
  Set byte 1 of 'the drawer' to 0xE9,
  a number called 'the drawer byte written by a hex literal' is byte 1 of 'the drawer',
  If 'the drawer byte written by a hex literal' is not 233 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-23: expected 233 got {'the drawer byte written by a hex literal'}", Exit 95. Print 'the drawer byte written by a hex literal',
  Set byte 7 of 'the drawer' to 'b',
  a number called 'the drawer byte written by a character literal' is byte 7 of 'the drawer',
  If 'the drawer byte written by a character literal' is not 98 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-24: expected 98 got {'the drawer byte written by a character literal'}", Exit 95. Print 'the drawer byte written by a character literal',
  Print 'the drawer byte written by a character literal'.

--- BUF-25: declare from a string, mutate one byte with a character literal, the printed content reflects it ---
a buffer called 'the mailbag' is "8em6zta0e8ksyca".
Set byte 8 of 'the mailbag' to 'i'.
a text called 'the mailbag content after the mutation' is 'the mailbag' as text.
If 'the mailbag' is not "8em6ztaie8ksyca" then, Print "ASSERT BUF-25: expected 8em6ztaie8ksyca got {'the mailbag content after the mutation'}", Exit 95. Print 'the mailbag'.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a buffer called 'the mailbag' is "8em6zta0e8ksyca",
  Set byte 8 of 'the mailbag' to 'i',
  a text called 'the mailbag content after the mutation' is 'the mailbag' as text,
  If 'the mailbag' is not "8em6ztaie8ksyca" then, Print "ASSERT BUF-25: expected 8em6ztaie8ksyca got {'the mailbag content after the mutation'}", Exit 95. Print 'the mailbag'.

--- BUF-26: an out-of-bounds read is refused and the captured value is 0 ---
a buffer called 'the waybill' is "ddwm8bviv4gkbksnijiqkcn00xw2ty4ma608waum".
a boolean called 'the waybill found an error already pending' is false.
On error Set 'the waybill found an error already pending' to true.
a boolean called 'the waybill out of range read refused' is false.
a number called 'the waybill out of range value' is byte 165 of 'the waybill'.
On error Set 'the waybill out of range read refused' to true.
If 'the waybill out of range read refused' is false then, Print "ASSERT BUF-26: expected 1 got {'the waybill out of range read refused'}", Exit 95. Print 'the waybill out of range read refused'.
If 'the waybill out of range value' is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-26: expected 0 got {'the waybill out of range value'}", Exit 95. Print 'the waybill out of range value'.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a buffer called 'the waybill' is "ddwm8bviv4gkbksnijiqkcn00xw2ty4ma608waum",
  a boolean called 'the waybill found an error already pending' is false,
  On error Set 'the waybill found an error already pending' to true,
  a boolean called 'the waybill out of range read refused' is false,
  a number called 'the waybill out of range value' is byte 165 of 'the waybill',
  On error Set 'the waybill out of range read refused' to true,
  If 'the waybill out of range read refused' is false then, Print "ASSERT BUF-26: expected 1 got {'the waybill out of range read refused'}", Exit 95. Print 'the waybill out of range read refused',
  If 'the waybill out of range value' is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-26: expected 0 got {'the waybill out of range value'}", Exit 95. Print 'the waybill out of range value'.

--- BUF-31, BUF-32, BUF-38: append/copy between two buffers, source unchanged by either ---
a buffer called workbench is "87jtvfq8f8jw2cmyrqfn5q92pt".
a buffer called 'the dispatch note' is "r64b1y92z0mj66819p56ne9ea3rxzux8j1w86".
append workbench to 'the dispatch note'.
a text called 'the dispatch note content after the append' is 'the dispatch note' as text.
If 'the dispatch note' is not "r64b1y92z0mj66819p56ne9ea3rxzux8j1w8687jtvfq8f8jw2cmyrqfn5q92pt" then, Print "ASSERT BUF-31: expected r64b1y92z0mj66819p56ne9ea3rxzux8j1w8687jtvfq8f8jw2cmyrqfn5q92pt got {'the dispatch note content after the append'}", Exit 95. Print 'the dispatch note'.
a text called 'the dispatch note unchanged after the append' is workbench as text.
If workbench is not "87jtvfq8f8jw2cmyrqfn5q92pt" then, Print "ASSERT BUF-38: expected 87jtvfq8f8jw2cmyrqfn5q92pt got {'the dispatch note unchanged after the append'}", Exit 95. Print workbench.
a buffer called ledger is "dkg0p26erxj4sr4o5c7y2fdd".
copy workbench to ledger.
a text called 'ledger content after the copy' is ledger as text.
If ledger is not "87jtvfq8f8jw2cmyrqfn5q92pt" then, Print "ASSERT BUF-32: expected 87jtvfq8f8jw2cmyrqfn5q92pt got {'ledger content after the copy'}", Exit 95. Print ledger.
a text called 'ledger unchanged after the copy' is workbench as text.
If workbench is not "87jtvfq8f8jw2cmyrqfn5q92pt" then, Print "ASSERT BUF-38: expected 87jtvfq8f8jw2cmyrqfn5q92pt got {'ledger unchanged after the copy'}", Exit 95. Print workbench.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a buffer called workbench is "87jtvfq8f8jw2cmyrqfn5q92pt",
  a buffer called 'the dispatch note' is "r64b1y92z0mj66819p56ne9ea3rxzux8j1w86",
  append workbench to 'the dispatch note',
  a text called 'the dispatch note content after the append' is 'the dispatch note' as text,
  If 'the dispatch note' is not "r64b1y92z0mj66819p56ne9ea3rxzux8j1w8687jtvfq8f8jw2cmyrqfn5q92pt" then, Print "ASSERT BUF-31: expected r64b1y92z0mj66819p56ne9ea3rxzux8j1w8687jtvfq8f8jw2cmyrqfn5q92pt got {'the dispatch note content after the append'}", Exit 95. Print 'the dispatch note',
  a text called 'the dispatch note unchanged after the append' is workbench as text,
  If workbench is not "87jtvfq8f8jw2cmyrqfn5q92pt" then, Print "ASSERT BUF-38: expected 87jtvfq8f8jw2cmyrqfn5q92pt got {'the dispatch note unchanged after the append'}", Exit 95. Print workbench,
  a buffer called ledger is "dkg0p26erxj4sr4o5c7y2fdd",
  copy workbench to ledger,
  a text called 'ledger content after the copy' is ledger as text,
  If ledger is not "87jtvfq8f8jw2cmyrqfn5q92pt" then, Print "ASSERT BUF-32: expected 87jtvfq8f8jw2cmyrqfn5q92pt got {'ledger content after the copy'}", Exit 95. Print ledger,
  a text called 'ledger unchanged after the copy' is workbench as text,
  If workbench is not "87jtvfq8f8jw2cmyrqfn5q92pt" then, Print "ASSERT BUF-38: expected 87jtvfq8f8jw2cmyrqfn5q92pt got {'ledger unchanged after the copy'}", Exit 95. Print workbench.

--- BUF-36: a dynamic destination buffer grows past its initial reserve under append or copy ---
Create a buffer called 'the message slip'.
a boolean called 'the message slip found an error already pending' is false.
On error Set 'the message slip found an error already pending' to true.
a boolean called 'the message slip overflowed' is false.
copy "" to 'the message slip'.
On error Set 'the message slip overflowed' to true.
If 'the message slip overflowed' then, Print "ASSERT BUF-36: expected 0 got {'the message slip overflowed'}", Exit 95. Print 'the message slip overflowed'.
If 'the message slip's size is not 4374 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-36: expected 4374 got {'the message slip's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the message slip's size.
Print 'the message slip's capacity.

--- the same leaf, a different seed (the other verb) ---
Create a buffer called 'the waybill'.
a boolean called 'the waybill found an error already pending' is false.
On error Set 'the waybill found an error already pending' to true.
a boolean called 'the waybill overflowed' is false.
append "" to 'the waybill'.
On error Set 'the waybill overflowed' to true.
If 'the waybill overflowed' then, Print "ASSERT BUF-36: expected 0 got {'the waybill overflowed'}", Exit 95. Print 'the waybill overflowed'.
If 'the waybill's size is not 4936 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-36: expected 4936 got {'the waybill's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the waybill's size.
Print 'the waybill's capacity.

